<title>ISRAEL: Samsung weighs setting up R&amp;D unit in Israel.</title>
<headline>Samsung weighs setting up R&amp;D unit in Israel.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsung Electronics of South Korea is considering setting up a research and development centre in Israel, the Israel Export Institute said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said a seven-person delegation, headed by Min Hyung Chung, a senior manager at Samsung Electronics, and Jong Goo Lee, the head of the company's technology group, visited Israel last week in order to make a final decision.</p>
<p>They visited companies specialising in telecommunications, multimedia, software and semiconductors.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
